Provides: x-window-manager
Description: minimal X11 window manager with vertical tabs, based on wm2
 wm2tj is a window manager based on wm2 (1997): every window gets a tab on
 its left edge with the title drawn bottom to top, a close button and a thin
 frame, and very little else.  On top of that it adds what a laptop needs
 today: titles in UTF-8 through Xft, maximise and minimise, virtual desktops,
 EWMH support for taskbars, pagers and docks, a root menu with folders and a
 search box, and a small configuration file that is re-read on SIGHUP.
 .
 This package contains the window manager, the "wm2tj" session for the
 display manager, the menu generator, the settings windows and wm2-swipe,
 which switches desktops with a three-finger touchpad swipe.

Package: wm2tj-bar
Architecture: any
